WEBVTT

00:02.300 --> 00:04.440
Let's give it our all again today!

00:04.440 --> 00:06.450
We have two medals now,

00:06.450 --> 00:08.750
so let's make sure we get three more and...

00:09.150 --> 00:10.680
H-Huh?

00:11.150 --> 00:13.700
It's... morning now, right?

00:13.700 --> 00:14.530
Yeah...

00:14.530 --> 00:16.370
What could have happened?

00:16.370 --> 00:19.040
My map's not displaying.

00:19.930 --> 00:21.130
Neither is mine.

00:21.130 --> 00:22.260
Same.

00:22.260 --> 00:25.540
Looks like messaging isn't working, either.

00:25.750 --> 00:29.850
There's no telling what might happen. 
Let's all stick together today.

00:29.850 --> 00:31.740
Yeah, I think that's—

00:32.140 --> 00:33.960
Guys, watch out!

00:48.920 --> 00:51.020
Where am I?

00:51.940 --> 00:55.100
Sally! Everyone!

00:57.030 --> 00:58.820
Oh, right... The map...

01:00.450 --> 01:02.810
I just have to do whatever I can.

01:02.810 --> 01:05.300
Do your best to stay alive, everyone!

01:07.770 --> 01:12.050
<b>Maxing Defense </b>and <b>New Teams</b>.

01:09.850 --> 01:12.050
Splitting us up right from the start, huh?

01:12.050 --> 01:13.760
Those admins are malicious.

01:14.170 --> 01:16.470
Maple will probably be okay,

01:16.470 --> 01:18.930
but I'm worried about May and Yui...

01:27.170 --> 01:28.230
Huh?

01:28.230 --> 01:30.940
I guess there was no need 
to poke my nose in, huh?

01:31.350 --> 01:32.890
Frederica?

01:33.470 --> 01:35.270
So it <i>was</i> you, Sally.

01:35.270 --> 01:37.780
Anyway, we've got an enemy in front of us!

01:37.780 --> 01:39.820
Oboro! [Fire Child]!

01:42.790 --> 01:44.210
[Multi-Firebolt]!

01:44.210 --> 01:46.050
Notes! [Singing Round]!

01:52.630 --> 01:55.340
Oboro! [Cross Fire]! [Shadow Clone]!

02:05.930 --> 02:08.780
Looks like... we don't need more defense?

02:08.780 --> 02:10.270
Okay, then, [Multi-Waterbolt]!

02:17.700 --> 02:19.530
Gotta finish up here, too!

02:19.740 --> 02:21.240
[Multi-Firebolt]!

02:21.240 --> 02:22.990
Notes, [Amplify]!

02:31.620 --> 02:33.380
Guess we managed to beat them.

02:33.380 --> 02:35.480
Payne and the rest are pretty far away,

02:35.480 --> 02:38.480
so I was wondering what I was gonna do alone.

02:38.480 --> 02:40.720
Huh? You know where your buddies are?

02:41.070 --> 02:44.040
Oh, I have a skill for that.

02:44.040 --> 02:46.180
Anyway, I was wondering...

02:46.390 --> 02:49.140
You want to fight together, right?

02:49.140 --> 02:52.510
Bingo! I mean, there are no downsides, right?

02:52.510 --> 02:54.150
And we're both alone.

02:55.400 --> 02:57.480
Okay, in that case...

02:57.480 --> 02:59.700
Yep. So that's that.

02:59.700 --> 03:00.700
Yep.

03:00.700 --> 03:03.300
You can't get in touch with 
your guildmates either, right?

03:03.300 --> 03:05.480
Just stick with me for a while.

03:05.480 --> 03:07.160
Okay, sure...

03:09.910 --> 03:12.510
Fireworks? Are they part of an event?

03:12.510 --> 03:17.060
That's our signal. We use 
it when something comes up.

03:17.060 --> 03:19.220
You can bring fireworks in here?

03:19.220 --> 03:19.880
Nah.

03:20.200 --> 03:24.010
That's just Maple setting off 
explosives she sticks on herself.

03:24.350 --> 03:26.220
Huh? Say what?

03:26.220 --> 03:28.720
H-Hey, wait up!

03:28.720 --> 03:32.050
Better hurry up, or I'll leave you behind!

03:32.050 --> 03:35.650
Jeez, you're so pushy!

03:40.020 --> 03:41.250
Turtle?

03:41.250 --> 03:45.070
I'm okay! I hope someone finds us fast.

03:45.070 --> 03:46.850
Okay, Syrup, you're up!

03:46.850 --> 03:48.040
Turtle!

03:48.040 --> 03:49.870
Syrup! [Spirit Cannon]!

03:51.070 --> 03:53.290
Tur...

03:53.290 --> 03:55.290
Okay, and now...

03:58.210 --> 04:01.470
D-Don't just show up right 
there! It's dangerous!

04:02.390 --> 04:03.380
Turtle?

04:11.110 --> 04:12.420
H-Huh?

04:13.880 --> 04:15.850
I see you're up to something crazy again,

04:16.510 --> 04:17.510
Maple.

04:17.890 --> 04:18.980
Mii!

04:22.020 --> 04:22.850
Run away!

04:22.850 --> 04:24.440
Move it! We'll get swallowed up!

04:24.440 --> 04:27.480
This is bad! Really bad!

04:30.840 --> 04:32.710
You okay? Can you stand up?

04:32.710 --> 04:35.120
I-It's no use!

04:35.120 --> 04:37.130
We're all gonna die!

04:37.130 --> 04:38.880
Keep it together!

04:39.110 --> 04:41.430
You're a strong man, aren't ya?

04:42.850 --> 04:45.550
We gotta run over there! You can run, right?

04:47.400 --> 04:49.560
Run! You have to run!

04:49.560 --> 04:53.600
Bro! This ain't the time for that!

04:55.320 --> 04:56.100
Uh-oh!

04:57.420 --> 04:59.150
What?! The whole map?

04:59.150 --> 05:03.430
Yeah. Seems it's being swallowed 
up by darkness from the outside in.

05:03.740 --> 05:06.410
It's already claimed several in my party.

05:06.410 --> 05:08.510
Okay. I'll be careful.

05:08.510 --> 05:11.410
I'll have to do something to thank you again.

05:11.410 --> 05:15.000
In that case, there's one 
thing I'd like to ask of you.

05:15.000 --> 05:16.620
Hold on to this.

05:16.840 --> 05:19.470
It will disappear once this event ends.

05:19.470 --> 05:23.590
What is... A "Marker Card"? 
That's really all you want?

05:28.540 --> 05:30.330
Yeah. Keep it, okay?

05:30.330 --> 05:33.010
It's an item Marcus made.

05:33.010 --> 05:35.700
If you have this, I'll know where you are.

05:35.700 --> 05:37.900
Oh, I get it! That's handy!

05:38.470 --> 05:41.020
Turtle!

05:42.180 --> 05:45.860
I hope we won't be enemies 
the next time we meet.

05:45.860 --> 05:46.950
Farewell!

05:46.950 --> 05:50.460
Yeah! Thanks! See you later!

05:50.460 --> 05:51.380
Sure!

05:55.620 --> 06:00.510
Okay! We gotta get back to 
setting off fireworks, Syrup!

06:00.510 --> 06:01.840
Turtle!

06:18.370 --> 06:21.010
Your companion's ability is amazing.

06:22.230 --> 06:26.190
Still, I can't believe the two logistics 
specialists were tossed into a dungeon.

06:26.190 --> 06:28.420
Depending on what the boss is, we're toast.

06:28.420 --> 06:29.700
We're in trouble.

06:29.700 --> 06:32.410
We'll be fine, Marcus the Trapper.

06:32.410 --> 06:34.160
I'll be counting on you.

06:35.350 --> 06:37.770
Flattery will get you nowhere.

06:50.380 --> 06:52.530
Can't we do anything 
about how many there are?

06:52.530 --> 06:55.230
There is an attribute that we 
can use against them, but...

06:55.230 --> 06:56.560
Bell, please!

07:04.150 --> 07:07.320
Man, I'm lucky I got paired 
up with a support like you.

07:07.640 --> 07:11.030
I'm also glad I ran into a 
shield user such as yourself.

07:11.280 --> 07:12.580
Well, thanks!

07:12.580 --> 07:14.950
Necro! [Burst Flame]!

07:18.410 --> 07:20.250
[Holy Spear]!

07:22.040 --> 07:23.280
[Revitalize]!

07:23.280 --> 07:25.630
Necro! [Armored: Strong]!

07:32.600 --> 07:34.410
We could stick it out, but...

07:34.410 --> 07:37.560
Try to stay strong.
It shouldn't be long now...

07:38.950 --> 07:40.060
There she is!

07:46.780 --> 07:47.980
Wow...

07:50.940 --> 07:53.610
Thank you, Mii.

07:53.610 --> 07:55.450
I'm glad you're safe.

07:55.450 --> 07:57.490
Oh? Kuromu is here, too?

07:57.490 --> 07:59.080
Yeah.

07:59.080 --> 08:02.210
Hey, did you see anyone from my guild?

08:02.210 --> 08:04.360
I saw Maple earlier.

08:04.360 --> 08:06.710
She was up to something crazy again.

08:06.710 --> 08:09.250
Oh... those fireworks, you mean?

08:09.250 --> 08:10.170
Fireworks?

08:11.400 --> 08:13.590
Never mind. We'll talk later.

08:13.590 --> 08:15.980
It seems Shin and Marcus 
are still alive, as well.

08:15.980 --> 08:17.140
We'll go find them.

08:17.140 --> 08:19.270
Yes, of course.

08:19.270 --> 08:21.600
Mind if I tag along with you?

08:21.600 --> 08:25.270
Before I ran into Misery, 
I saw a few other players.

08:25.270 --> 08:28.770
Running into this many players 
on such a big playing field

08:29.160 --> 08:33.830
must mean everyone's getting 
sent to roughly the same points.

08:33.830 --> 08:34.950
I see.

08:34.950 --> 08:39.920
So you think the members of Maple Tree 
might be near where our guildmates are?

08:39.920 --> 08:43.250
It's only a possibility, but 
it beats searching blindly.

08:43.250 --> 08:44.870
What about Maple?

08:44.870 --> 08:48.510
Our leader will be okay 
on her own for a while.

08:49.540 --> 08:51.190
You do have a point.

08:51.190 --> 08:53.590
And we would appreciate having 
a shield user with us.

08:53.590 --> 08:56.600
I suppose we'll be working 
together a bit longer, then.

08:56.600 --> 08:58.340
I look forward to adventuring with you.

08:58.340 --> 09:00.310
Yeah, same here.

09:16.910 --> 09:19.120
[Remote Trap - Wind Strike]!

09:21.490 --> 09:22.420
Now!

09:22.420 --> 09:23.330
[Change]!

09:31.170 --> 09:34.550
Oh, hey! It's easy to aim 
when they're this close!

09:34.550 --> 09:36.800
All cannons, fire!

09:55.030 --> 09:56.580
What was that?

09:56.580 --> 10:00.240
Probably our Crafter.
She's scary when she's angry.

10:03.030 --> 10:05.780
Hey, Iz! Looks like you're okay!

10:06.160 --> 10:07.620
Oh? Kuromu?

10:07.620 --> 10:09.910
Mii! Thank goodness!

10:09.910 --> 10:11.630
I'm glad you're safe, Marcus.

10:11.840 --> 10:14.590
I was worried when your signal disappeared.

10:14.590 --> 10:16.070
Oh, yeah...

10:16.070 --> 10:19.930
A lot happened, but I came out 
okay in the end... I guess.

10:19.930 --> 10:23.010
We just beat a boss and got medals.

10:24.110 --> 10:27.130
I got a notification. Good work.

10:27.130 --> 10:29.020
You two beat it on your own?

10:30.280 --> 10:33.320
We made a good team! Right?

10:33.320 --> 10:37.330
With your firepower, I'm sure you're more 
than capable of fighting on your own.

10:37.330 --> 10:41.620
Oh, not at all! 
I'm just a Crafter, after all!

10:41.860 --> 10:44.280
Having you there was a huge help, Marcus!

10:46.920 --> 10:49.360
I can't believe they multiply 
twofold when slain.

10:49.360 --> 10:50.970
How many are left?

10:50.970 --> 10:53.090
Man, there's no end to these guys.

10:55.300 --> 10:57.640
Looks like I'm up now.

10:57.640 --> 10:59.760
Yes. I'm counting on you, Shin.

11:01.260 --> 11:03.220
Wen! [Wind God]!

11:07.530 --> 11:09.060
[Split-Sword]!

11:13.820 --> 11:16.400
Big numbers aren't enough to beat... me?!

11:20.310 --> 11:21.800
[Purple Phantom Blade]!

11:29.830 --> 11:32.740
Thanks. You saved my skin.

11:33.270 --> 11:34.770
That aside...

11:36.500 --> 11:39.020
You look as adorable as ever.

11:39.020 --> 11:41.470
Shut up! Keep staring and I'll slash you!

11:46.390 --> 11:48.990
Guess we managed to get out alive.

11:48.990 --> 11:53.730
But even if I hook up with Mii 
now, we've lost our base... huh?

11:56.750 --> 12:01.100
Hey! Hey! Over here! Hey!

11:58.600 --> 12:01.100
S-Stop! They'll see us!

12:01.100 --> 12:03.230
I <i>want</i> them to find us!

12:03.230 --> 12:05.110
Come on, Kasumi, join me!

12:07.630 --> 12:11.320
Hey! Hey!

12:11.320 --> 12:13.080
Hey...

12:24.530 --> 12:28.140
Thanks for the help. I might not 
have survived this on my own.

12:28.440 --> 12:29.810
Yeah, right.

12:29.810 --> 12:33.850
But hey, having a support made 
this easy for me. So thanks.

12:34.170 --> 12:36.260
You two stay hidden a bit longer.

12:36.260 --> 12:38.950
I can't cover for you both like Maple can.

12:38.950 --> 12:40.470
S-Sorry about this.

12:40.470 --> 12:42.070
Thank you so much.

12:42.070 --> 12:44.950
Looks like Frederica's 
headed this way, too...

12:44.950 --> 12:46.620
but we can talk later!

12:46.620 --> 12:48.700
Agreed! [Fireball]!

12:51.360 --> 12:52.580
[Earth Surge]!

12:58.080 --> 12:59.160
Wow!

12:59.160 --> 13:02.920
If we could do that, we could've 
put up more of a fight.

13:02.920 --> 13:06.140
We all have things we're good 
at and things we're bad at.

13:06.140 --> 13:09.370
You just have to wait until the time 
comes for you to show what you can do.

13:09.370 --> 13:10.460
R-Right!

13:10.460 --> 13:12.870
Whoops! [Protective Barrier]!

13:15.910 --> 13:19.190
Nice guarding! You're every 
bit as good as Frederica!

13:19.190 --> 13:23.440
Keep talking like that and I'm 
not gonna help you anymore.

13:23.440 --> 13:26.690
Oh, you're here already? That 
was quicker than I thought.

13:26.690 --> 13:29.320
Oh, and Sally's with you, too?

13:29.320 --> 13:32.290
This is where you were? And May and Yui, too?

13:32.290 --> 13:35.870
Yes. We almost made it to where Maple was,

13:35.870 --> 13:38.100
but we're just so slow...

13:38.100 --> 13:42.300
Yui, the battle's still going on!
 There's no time to chat!

13:42.300 --> 13:45.600
Hmm... I think we're good now, actually.

13:45.600 --> 13:46.260
Huh?

13:46.260 --> 13:47.700
[Sword of Judgment]!

13:47.700 --> 13:49.140
[Whirlwind Flurry]!

13:54.810 --> 13:56.430
I'm glad you're safe.

13:56.430 --> 13:59.540
Didn't expect to see you 
guys with them, though.

13:59.540 --> 14:01.570
Payne! Dread!

14:01.570 --> 14:04.240
You guys have gotten a lot stronger.

14:04.240 --> 14:07.080
I'm glad the main event wasn't PVP.

14:07.080 --> 14:08.660
Where are the other members?

14:08.660 --> 14:10.910
Not many of them left.

14:10.910 --> 14:13.580
Apparently the base got 
swallowed up ages ago.

14:13.830 --> 14:16.280
So we'll have to start over 
with finding a location...

14:16.280 --> 14:20.570
Damn, what a pain. We put a 
lot of work into that base.

14:20.570 --> 14:22.140
Nothing we can do.

14:22.140 --> 14:25.690
Gonna be hard to keep exploring 
continuously without a base.

14:29.720 --> 14:30.720
Um, hey...

14:30.720 --> 14:33.470
I'd like to negotiate with you a bit.

14:33.470 --> 14:34.750
Is that all right?

14:38.940 --> 14:39.690
Huh?

14:39.690 --> 14:41.400
What does that mean?

14:41.400 --> 14:44.340
Basically, we would offer the use of our base

14:44.340 --> 14:46.840
and have everyone go there with us.

14:46.840 --> 14:49.110
I was thinking the same thing.

14:49.110 --> 14:50.860
What do you say, Guildmaster?

14:51.990 --> 14:55.870
I like it! With everyone there, we can 
beat any monsters that come for us!

14:55.870 --> 14:57.980
Besides, the more the merrier!

14:57.980 --> 14:58.830
Turtle!

14:58.830 --> 15:01.950
We'll be barging in for a little while, then.

15:02.500 --> 15:04.620
We can't offer any real hospitality, though.

15:04.620 --> 15:06.360
Maple's base, huh?

15:06.360 --> 15:08.200
There aren't any weird traps, are there?

15:08.200 --> 15:11.150
Nah! I'm sure it's probably mostly safe!

15:11.150 --> 15:12.300
Probably?

15:12.300 --> 15:16.610
Yeah, but you guys set up your base 
right in the middle of the map.

15:16.610 --> 15:17.890
Isn't that a little too perfect?

15:19.000 --> 15:22.450
That was pure chance. I think it's just 
because Maple's got such good luck.

15:22.450 --> 15:24.610
Maple is amazing!

15:24.610 --> 15:27.160
Sorry to impose with such a large group.

15:27.160 --> 15:31.690
It's okay! It'll be even more fun 
with lots of friends around, I bet!

15:32.490 --> 15:36.600
Thank you. The rest of our guild 
members should be here soon, as well.

15:36.600 --> 15:38.380
Boss!

15:40.840 --> 15:43.180
Looks like they're all still alive.

15:43.180 --> 15:46.210
Those guys have the devil's luck.

15:47.230 --> 15:51.130
Okay, I guess it's time to 
show everyone to our base!

15:51.130 --> 15:53.890
We'll be okay on space,

15:53.890 --> 15:56.900
but we need to make sure each guild 
can use the facilities as needed.

15:57.870 --> 15:59.750
I'll have to make a few things!

15:59.750 --> 16:02.610
Time to show off my Crafter skills!

16:02.610 --> 16:04.310
Ooh, Iz is really...

16:04.310 --> 16:05.650
...on fire!

16:45.770 --> 16:49.410
Well, it's just about time to 
release the day two monsters!

16:49.410 --> 16:53.570
Yeah. The forced relocation 
took out a lot of players.

16:53.570 --> 16:56.430
Now we'll give them a series 
of back-to-back trials!

16:56.430 --> 16:59.850
All the players are still 
pretty scattered, too.

16:59.850 --> 17:02.580
They won't complain that we're 
being unfair again, will they?

17:02.580 --> 17:04.120
Uh... N-No way!

17:04.120 --> 17:06.090
We divided them up by 
difficulty level this time,

17:06.090 --> 17:10.840
and the event wouldn't be fun if the 
highest difficulty was that easy to beat.

17:11.580 --> 17:13.010
Hey! Look at this!

17:13.010 --> 17:15.340
Is that more than two parties in one place?!

17:15.340 --> 17:16.790
Where <i>is</i> that?

17:16.790 --> 17:20.260
A dungeon made even more deadly 
by the players: Maple Tree.

17:18.950 --> 17:24.980
Secretary

17:20.260 --> 17:23.680
The surviving members of Order of 
the Holy Sword and Flame Emperors

17:23.680 --> 17:24.980
have joined them there.

17:24.980 --> 17:27.250
Why? How?

17:27.250 --> 17:29.310
There's more of them! There's more of them!

17:29.310 --> 17:32.920
Sending all of tonight's monsters 
there would be too cruel...

17:32.920 --> 17:34.060
for the monsters.

17:34.060 --> 17:36.450
But we can't stop them! Look!

17:36.450 --> 17:39.200
We did all the thinking 
and adjusting we could

17:39.200 --> 17:42.710
to minimize the number of players 
that complete this event.

17:42.710 --> 17:48.790
Yeah. We sent strong monsters, we destroyed 
bases, we made maps unusable...

17:48.790 --> 17:53.210
And we added completion prizes 
appropriate to the difficulty level.

17:53.210 --> 17:56.260
But if the three top guilds 
are working together,

17:56.260 --> 17:59.930
a lot more people are gonna 
complete it than we planned for!

17:59.930 --> 18:02.080
And what happens if they do?

18:02.080 --> 18:03.460
You don't know?

18:04.230 --> 18:06.510
We'll have to keep making adjustments.

18:10.770 --> 18:12.890
Oh? What's that?

18:12.890 --> 18:15.160
Uh, it's...

18:18.150 --> 18:20.390
Ooh, wow!

18:20.390 --> 18:22.030
A-As long as it's within sight,

18:22.030 --> 18:26.160
we can tell what types of traps have been 
reset and how strong any monsters are.

18:27.320 --> 18:29.810
It's boring just waiting around.

18:29.810 --> 18:31.540
You've sure settled in.

18:31.540 --> 18:34.590
Well, I've been to Maple 
Tree lots of times before.

18:34.590 --> 18:37.790
That's just how many times Sally's 
beaten you at your own game, huh?

18:37.790 --> 18:38.930
Grr!

18:39.160 --> 18:41.060
Looks like something's coming in.

18:54.770 --> 18:57.010
That one will make it all the way in here.

18:57.010 --> 18:59.210
It looks a lot stronger than yesterday's.

18:59.210 --> 19:00.280
Payne!

19:00.280 --> 19:01.710
There's work to do!

19:02.090 --> 19:05.620
Right. I'll do my share of work 
to cover our stay at their base.

19:05.620 --> 19:06.860
I'll go, as well.

19:07.290 --> 19:09.790
We'll save the rest of you for later.

19:10.370 --> 19:12.910
Don't be stingy with your strength, Payne.

19:12.910 --> 19:14.790
Yes, of course.

19:14.790 --> 19:16.000
Alrighty!

19:16.220 --> 19:18.700
I'll just put some buffs on you, then.

19:18.700 --> 19:19.970
Go get 'em!

19:19.970 --> 19:22.680
Be careful, you two!

19:26.600 --> 19:27.670
Ignis!

19:27.670 --> 19:30.440
[Phoenix Flame]! [Become Fire]!

19:31.020 --> 19:34.060
Ray! [Torrent of Light!]! 
[Release All Magic]!

19:41.780 --> 19:43.490
[Karmic Fire of Carnage]!

19:43.740 --> 19:45.280
[Holy Dragon Light Blade]!

20:02.840 --> 20:05.180
Jeez, you guys!

20:05.180 --> 20:08.090
You took out Marcus's camera 
along with that monster!

20:08.090 --> 20:10.410
I didn't know we had a 
buff to extend our range.

20:10.410 --> 20:11.380
Sorry.

20:11.380 --> 20:13.390
Y-Yes, I apologize.

20:13.390 --> 20:16.140
That's a pretty rare item, too...

20:16.140 --> 20:18.530
That's such a shame, Marcus.

20:18.530 --> 20:22.070
And it'll take a long time to reset it.

20:22.070 --> 20:23.540
What do I do now?

20:24.500 --> 20:29.640
It'll be pretty inefficient to keep 
resetting our traps and cameras every time.

20:29.640 --> 20:31.200
What should we do, then?

20:31.200 --> 20:33.970
I think we can just intercept 
most monsters that show up.

20:33.970 --> 20:38.420
The ones that attacked us tonight 
didn't seem all that strong.

20:38.700 --> 20:42.670
Right. In that case, we should 
go out and conquer dungeons

20:42.670 --> 20:45.010
to secure as many medals 
as possible while we can.

20:45.010 --> 20:47.320
What? We should go outside?

20:47.320 --> 20:51.220
Considering the way we were 
all forcibly relocated today,

20:51.220 --> 20:54.350
there's a good chance something will 
happen in the morning, as well.

20:54.580 --> 20:58.060
Between the second morning and the third 
morning, it should be easy to guess

20:58.060 --> 20:59.500
which will be more dangerous.

21:00.430 --> 21:02.300
So you had the same idea.

21:02.300 --> 21:04.360
We're missing many of our guild members,

21:04.360 --> 21:06.110
but I think we should be proactive.

21:06.110 --> 21:08.660
In that case, we'll help, too!

21:08.660 --> 21:10.490
Wha... Maple?!

21:12.110 --> 21:14.430
It'll be easier to fight that way, right?

21:15.450 --> 21:19.130
Well, you heard our guildmaster. 
What do you say?

21:20.840 --> 21:22.430
We couldn't ask for more.

21:25.380 --> 21:30.350
Okay, so May, Yui, Marcus, 
and Dread will go east.

21:30.350 --> 21:34.560
Payne, Misery, Iz, and Kanade will go west.

21:34.560 --> 21:39.020
Drag, Shin, Kuromu, and Kasumi will go south.

21:39.020 --> 21:44.490
And that leaves me, Maple, Mii, 
and Frederica to go north.

21:44.710 --> 21:45.710
And we...

21:45.710 --> 21:47.450
...will stay behind...

21:47.450 --> 21:49.070
...in the name of defending the base!

21:49.070 --> 21:52.870
We will defeat any invading monsters, 
however strong they may be!

21:54.040 --> 21:56.270
Our goal is to get medals!

21:56.270 --> 21:59.000
Let's get as many as we can 
before the night's over!

21:59.000 --> 22:00.980
Yeah!

